{title: Immortal, Invisible, God Only Wise}
{artist: Walter Chalmers Smith}
{key: G}
{time: 3/4}
{tempo: 108}

Verse 1
Im[G]mortal, in[C]visible, [G]God only [D]wise,
in [G]light inac[C]cessible [G]hid [D]from our [G]eyes,
most blessed, most [C]glorious, the [G]Ancient of [D]Days,
al[G]mighty, vic[C]torious, thy [G]great [D]name we [G]praise.

Verse 2
Unresting, [G]unhasting, and [G]silent as [D]light,
Nor [G]wanting, nor [C]wasting, [G]Thou [D]rulest in [G]might;
Thy justice, like [C]mountains, [G]high soaring [D]above
Thy [G]clouds, which [C]are fountains [G]of [D]goodness and [G]love.

Verse 3
To [G]all, life Thou [C]givest, to [G]both great and [D]small;
In [G]all life Thou [C]livest, [G]the [D]true life of [G]all;
We blossom and [C]flourish as leaves [G]on the [D]tree,
And [G]wither and [C]perish [G]but [D]naught changeth [G]Thee.

Verse 4
Great [G]Father of [C]glory, pure [G]Father of [D]light,
Thine [G]angels adore [C]Thee, [G]all [D]veiling their [G]sight;
But of Thy [C]rich graces this [G]grace, Lord, [D]impart
Take [G]the veil from [C]our face, [G]the [D]vile from our [G]heart.

Verse 5
All [G]laud we would [C]render; O [G]help us to [D]see
'Tis [G]only the [C]splendor [G]of [D]light hideth [G]Thee,
And so let [C]Thy [G]glory, almighty, [D]impart,
Through [G]Christ in [C]His story, Thy [G]Christ [D]to the [G]heart.
